    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d719">

                <pb facs="0704" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg588"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 294.11Ei5/1.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Ambassador
                    Guthrie</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-09-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 25, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Request arrest and provisional detention of John Eills, charged with perjury in
                    Massachusetts, where a warrant has been issued for his arrest. The Governor of
                    Massachusetts has been informed that Eills is at Tokio. It is feared that
                    accused may do violence to himself or his daughter, who is with him. Endeavor to
                    have this prevented, Formal papers have already gone forward, and officers will
                    proceed at once to Japan on learning of arrest.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
